$OnExit=X,Tell,Blank
</?>
<?!{param.1}>
$OnExit=X,Tell,Blank
</?>

[***********************************************************]
[DemoNote]
<h2>Demonstration</h2>
<p>
This is a demonstration of NetStorm, version {version}. 
<p>
This demo has three missions, all the tutorials, and lets you play
in Multiplayer using only Sun Knowledge. Save games created during this
demo can be continued when you purchase the game!
<p>
Hit F1 in the game for help and technical support.
<p>
Have fun!

$Button=OK,Tell,{param.1}

[***********************************************************]
[TipList]
tip0="You can use <c>F2</c> to make bridge connecting easier."
tip1="You can <c>right-click</c> on anything to get help about it - even game windows!"
tip2="You can use <c>F5</c> to find your Priest at any time."
tip3="You can check the range of enemy units by clicking on them."
tip4="When you place a unit off of a bridge, you can build more bridge from that unit's island!"
tip5="If you build bridge directly to a Geyser it's harder to connect than if you approach from one side."
tip6="You should always continue building bridges to Storm Geysers so that your Golems never stop harvesting."
tip7="When forming a bridge arm for attack you can alternate your branch arms in and out to maximize mobility, offensive, and defensive positioning!"
tip8="Towers can be used to protect weak attack units!"
tip9="You get Storm Power every time you destroy an enemy unit!"
tip10="Once you've attached to a Geyser you own its island, and can build bridge off of it!"
tip11="Building more Workshops is more efficient than Upgrading!"
tip12="A mix of weapons is often better than focusing on just one type."
tip13="All units will always pick the closest available target - even if its invulnerable to their attack!"
tip14="When transports arrive at an empty Geyser, they always choose the Geyser closest to your Temple next - even if it is in enemy territory!"
tip15="You shouldn't cluster your shooting units together - when one blows up they will all be damaged!"
tip16="You can break through enemy bridge by building an inexpensive unit right next to it, and then Salvaging your unit. The destructive force will cause normal bridge to crack, and cracked bridge to crumble!"
tip17="If you have a fast video card you may be able to use <c>Options / Adjust Direct Draw / Parallax Clouds</c> in Direct Draw mode. Its cool!!"
tip18="When shooting an enemy unit, aim for the area where it meets the ground. If you try to hit it up high your shots may pass right by it!"
tip19="You can build on your allies' Island and bridges, if your bridges connect."
tip20="You can Salvage what you're not using when you need extra Storm Power."
tip21="Since units always choose the closest target, you can often use Towers to distract enemy fire while you attack from another angle!"
tip22="Beware of broken bridges! Golems may walk off a bridge if it existed when they started moving!"
tip23="The Priest can Pray for a powerful Spell in multiplayer games!"
tip24="You can build Outposts in Multiplayer Mode to control more islands!"
tip25="Air units can not attack other air units!"
tip26="Which 'slot' you choose in a Multiplayer Challenge Ring determines the location of your island in the battle."
tip27="The key to fighting Whirligigs, Dust Devils, and Man o' Wars is to kill their bases - never waste time on the flyers themselves."
tip28="If you don't want to have to worry about running out of money, use Sun units - they're cheap!"
tip29="Each Transport has important differences - if you know how to use them creatively!"
tip30="You can group weapons in a complementary manner.  The weakness of one could be the strength of the other!"
tip31="You can build more bridge even when the one you're connecting to is still dark."
tip32="You can visit Activision and Titanic's web sites for important updates and technical support."
tip33="In Multiplayer, if you start typing another player's name in the chat window and hit TAB, it will fill in the rest of the name."
tip34="You're out of Tips!<$Config,tipNumber=0>"

[***********************************************************]
[AllianceRequested]
<h2>Alliance Requested</h2>
<c>{param.1}</c> would like to form an Alliance. If you agree, you 
will be able to build off each other's bridges and your Battle Units will 
not target each other.

<p>
Do you agree to the Alliance?
$Button=Yes,ConfirmAlliance,{param.2}
$Button=No,DoNothing,0

[***********************************************************]
[AllianceComplete]
<h2>Alliance Complete</h2>
You and <c>{param.1}</c> are now mutual Allies. You can both build off each 
other's bridges, and your Battle Units will not target each other.
<p>
Note that you still have be connected to your Ally's bridge network to be 
able to build off of it!
$Button=OK,DoNothing,0

[***********************************************************]
[AllianceBroken]
<h2>Alliance Broken</h2>
Your Alliance with <c>{param.1}</c> is now broken!
$Button=OK,DoNothing,0

